{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794732322,"nonce":"EEPpIK+xbxFskIBqHnyyjny5AWY=","message":"Decided (2026-11-15), aiming for what's legally needed rather than full TASL:\n- One flat table attribution (id, author, licence, source); user_document and user_document_annotation reference it by attribution_id instead of carrying the three columns. No creators list or roles, no licence table, no note.\n- Rows are content-addressed: id is a hash of {author, licence, source}, INSERT OR IGNORE, no owner, never updated. annotationId keeps hashing the same fields, so ids only change where a licence gets its versioned id.\n- licence is a CHECK on attribution.licence with versioned values (cc-by-3.0, cc-by-4.0, ...); deed links stay in LICENCE_INFO. Existing values become their 4.0 ids, then the 3.0 stories' files and their narration get theirs.\n- The two shareable rules (a public entry needs a shareable licence; an annotation's licence is shareable) move to the API only, since they now cross tables.\n- The API's JSON keeps licence, author and source flat.\n- Open: delete attribution rows nothing references, or leave them.\n\nResearch (CC BY 3.0 4(a)/4(b), BY 4.0 3(a), CC's recommended practices, a Storybooks page, Wolne Lektury's zasady-wykorzystania) gave these gaps, independent of the table:\n- The reader shows no credit for annotations, but plays the 420 CC BY narration clips. Show their distinct credits under the text's (e.g. 'Recordings: Helena Gabriela, CC BY 3.0, source').\n- Name the African Storybook original in the Storybooks author lines (as above).\n- Revert the Liczymy zwierzęta typo fix.\n- Show the source link as its site name or domain rather than 'source' (covers Wolne Lektury's ask).\n- wolneLekturyLicence drops the licence's version; the sync ignores the API's translators (none of the 17 synced texts has one today).","files":null}]}